  "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Agentic Coding Research Report - 2026-05-24</title>\n    <style>\n        * {\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 10pt;\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            color: #000000;\n            line-height: 1.4;\n        }\n\n        .container {\n            max-width: 1200px;\n            margin: 0 auto;\n            padding: 10px;\n        }\n\n        header {\n            background-color: #ff6600;\n            padding: 5px 10px;\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n        }\n\n        header h1 {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 14pt;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        header .date {\n            font-size: 9pt;\n            margin-top: 3px;\n        }\n\n        .three-column-layout {\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: 40% 35% 25%;\n            gap: 15px;\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\n        }\n\n        @media (max-width: 1024px) {\n            .three-column-layout {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n            }\n        }\n\n        section {\n            background-color: #ffffff;\n            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            padding: 10px;\n        }\n\n        section h2 {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 12pt;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 12px;\n            padding-bottom: 5px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        .item {\n            margin-bottom: 12px;\n            padding-bottom: 10px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #eeeeee;\n        }\n\n        .item:last-child {\n            border-bottom: none;\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n            padding-bottom: 0;\n        }\n\n        .item-title {\n            font-size: 10pt;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 4px;\n        }\n\n        .item-title a {\n            color: #000000;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        .item-title a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        .item-title a:visited {\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .item-description {\n            font-size: 9pt;\n            color: #000000;\n            margin-bottom: 4px;\n            line-height: 1.4;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta {\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .tag {\n            display: inline-block;\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            padding: 1px 4px;\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            margin-right: 3px;\n            margin-top: 3px;\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .update-type {\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: #ff6600;\n            margin-right: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .product-name {\n            font-size: 9pt;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: #828282;\n            margin-bottom: 2px;\n        }\n\n        .source-badge {\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            color: #828282;\n            font-style: italic;\n        }\n\n        .topics {\n            margin-top: 5px;\n        }\n\n        footer {\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            padding: 10px;\n            text-align: center;\n            font-size: 9pt;\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        footer a {\n            color: #000000;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        footer a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        .empty-section {\n            font-style: italic;\n            color: #828282;\n            text-align: center;\n            padding: 20px;\n        }\n\n        .highlight {\n            background-color: #ffffd0;\n            padding: 0 2px;\n        }\n\n        @media print {\n            body {\n                background-color: #ffffff;\n            }\n\n            .three-column-layout {\n                display: block;\n            }\n\n            section {\n                page-break-inside: avoid;\n                margin-bottom: 20px;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <header>\n            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n            <div class=\"date\">2026-05-24 | Daily Update on AI-Powered Development Tools</div>\n        </header>\n\n        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n            <!-- New Products Section (40%) -->\n            <section class=\"new-products\">\n                <h2>New Products</h2>\n                <div class=\"empty-section\">\n                    No new products discovered today. Check back tomorrow for the latest tools and platforms in the agentic coding space.\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35%) -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                <h2>Product Updates</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[RELEASE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\">Copilot for Eclipse Open Source</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub Copilot for Eclipse is now open source, making the codebase available for community contribution and transparency.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-21</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[FEATURE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\">Semantic Issue Search in Copilot Chat</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub released semantic issue search functionality in Copilot Chat, enabling more intelligent code issue discovery and resolution.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-20</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[FEATURE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\">Auto Model Selection Based on Task in VS Code</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Copilot now automatically routes to appropriate models based on the specific task being performed in VS Code, improving efficiency and accuracy.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-20</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[RELEASE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\">Gemini 3.5 Flash Generally Available</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google's Gemini 3.5 Flash model is now generally available for GitHub Copilot users, providing faster AI assistance.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-19</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[RELEASE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\">GPT-5.3-Codex Base Model for Business and Enterprise</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GPT-5.3-Codex is now the base model for Copilot Business and Enterprise tiers, offering improved coding capabilities.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-17</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[FEATURE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\">Team-level Usage Metrics via API</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Team-level Copilot usage metrics are now available via API, giving organizations better visibility into AI adoption and spending.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-14</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[RELEASE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\">GitHub Copilot App Technical Preview</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub released a new Copilot app in technical preview, expanding Copilot's accessibility and integration options.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-14</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">Devin</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[FEATURE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\">Platform Default Settings and Slack Improvements</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Devin added platform default settings (Linux/Windows) for sessions, Slack channel override functionality, and MCP OAuth resource parameter support.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-15</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">Devin</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[FEATURE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\">GitLab Interactive PR Review</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitLab repositories now support interactive PR review in Devin, with the ability to post review comments and resolve threads when read-write GitLab connection is enabled.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-10</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">Gemini CLI</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[ANNOUNCEMENT]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.googleblog.com/an-important-update-transitioning-gemini-cli-to-antigravity-cli/\">Deprecation Notice - Transitioning to Antigravity CLI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google announced Gemini CLI will stop serving requests on June 18, 2026, transitioning users to Antigravity CLI.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-10</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">Gemini CLI</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[FEATURE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://releasebot.io/updates/google/gemini-cli\">May 2026 Update - Command Line and UI Improvements</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Gemini CLI shipped a broad update with command line improvements, core and UI improvements, new session deletion options, commands listing options, and voice mode upgrades.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-08</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[FEATURE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\">Background Agents in Slack Integration</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Cursor now supports launching Background Agents directly from Slack by mentioning @Cursor. Agents can read threads, understand context, and create PRs without leaving Slack.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-15</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[FEATURE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\">BugBot Automatic Code Review</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Cursor 1.0 introduced BugBot for automatic code review that catches potential bugs and issues in PRs, leaving comments directly on GitHub with 'Fix in Cursor' integration.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-10</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[RELEASE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\">Background Agent General Availability</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Cursor's remote coding agent (Background Agent) is now available to all users, allowing parallel task execution with cloud icon in chat or Cmd/Ctrl+E shortcut.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-08</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type\">[FEATURE]</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\">Memories Feature Beta</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Cursor introduced Memories beta feature that allows the AI to remember facts from conversations and reference them in future sessions, stored per project at individual level.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-05-05</div>\n                </div>\n\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.windowscentral.com/microsoft/microsoft-cancels-claude-code-licenses-shifting-developers-to-github-copilot-cli-a-move-likely-driven-by-financial-motives\">Microsoft Cancels Claude Code Licenses</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Microsoft began canceling Claude Code licenses for thousands of developers across Windows, Microsoft 365, Outlook, and other teams. Decision driven by financial motives with deadline of June 30, 2026.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Windows Central / HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Microsoft</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Enterprise AI</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://kanbots.dev\">Kanbots: Open Source Kanban with Parallel AI Agents</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Kanbots v1.0 launched as open source (MIT licensed) kanban board running parallel Claude Code or Codex agents on every card, each in its own git worktree. Includes MCP server integration.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Open source</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://deno.com/blog/v2.8\">Deno 2.8 Released</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Deno 2.8 released with updates to the JavaScript/TypeScript runtime.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Deno team / HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Deno</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">JavaScript</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">TypeScript</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp\">Bun Support Deprecated in yt-dlp</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        The yt-dlp project announced that Bun support is now limited and deprecated, reflecting ongoing challenges in JavaScript runtime ecosystem compatibility.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">yt-dlp team / HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Bun</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Deprecation</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/superset-sh/superset\">Superset: IDE for the Agents Era (YC P26)</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Superset launched as an 'IDE for the agents era' from Y Combinator P26 batch, positioning itself as a development environment designed for AI agent workflows.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Superset / YC / HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">IDE</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">YC</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://anthropic.com\">Project Glasswing: Anthropic Update</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic published an initial update on Project Glasswing, trending on Hacker News with significant community interest.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Anthropic / HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Anthropic</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Research</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">The Memory Shortage and AI Impact</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon highlighted David Oks' explanation of how AI data centers are causing memory shortages. HBM allocation increasing from 2% to 20% by end of 2026, causing consumer electronics to become more expensive.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Simon Willison / Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI infrastructure</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">HBM</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Hardware</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">FTC Settlement on 'Active Listening' AI Fraud</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        FTC announced Cox Media Group will pay nearly $1 million to settle charges about deceiving customers regarding 'Active Listening' AI-powered marketing. Service actually just resold email lists from data brokers.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Simon Willison / Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI ethics</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Privacy</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">FTC</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Datasette Agent: First Release</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon announced Datasette Agent, a new extensible AI assistant integrating LLM capabilities with Datasette. Features include running commands in Fly Sprites sandbox and 'View SQL query' buttons.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Simon Willison / Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Datasette</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Python</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">SpaceX-Anthropic Deal: $1.25B/Month</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        SpaceX entered into Cloud Services Agreements with Anthropic for compute capacity across COLOSSUS and COLOSSUS II. Anthropic agreed to pay $1.25 billion per month through May 2029.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Simon Willison / Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI infrastructure</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Anthropic</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">SpaceX</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">How Fast is 10 Tokens Per Second?</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon highlighted an interactive HTML app that simulates LLM token output speeds from 5/second to 800/second, helping users understand what different token speeds actually feel like.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Simon Willison / Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">LLM performance</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Token speed</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Gemini 3.5 Flash: Prompt Injection Concerns</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google released Gemini 3.5 Flash and announced Gemini Spark personal AI agent. Simon expressed concerns about prompt injection risks, noting Gemini Spark will route traffic through Agent Gateway enforcing DLP policies.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Simon Willison / Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Google I/O</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Gemini</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI security</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Gemini 3.5 Flash: Pricing and Strategy</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon analyzed Google's release of Gemini 3.5 Flash at Google I/O 2026, noting it went straight to general availability without preview and Google is using it across many key products.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Simon Willison / Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Google</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Gemini</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">LLM pricing</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">LLM Lightning Talk at PyCon US 2026</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon presented a lightning talk at PyCon US 2026 with annotated slides covering the last six months of developments in the LLM space, providing rapid-fire overview of key trends.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Simon Willison / Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">LLMs</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">PyCon</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI trends</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">UK GDS on AI, Open Code and Vulnerability Risk</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        UK Government Digital Service published guidance stating 'Keep open by default' in response to NHS's decision to close open source repositories after vulnerability reports. GDS noted making everything private adds costs and reduces scrutiny.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta source-badge\">Simon Willison / Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Open source</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI security</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Government policy</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n            </section>\n        </main>\n\n        <footer>\n            <p>\n                <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> |\n                <a href=\"#\">About</a> |\n                <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a> |\n                Generated by AgentDaily\n            </p>\n            <p style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 8pt;\">\n                Covering the agentic coding revolution | Updated daily\n            </p>\n        </footer>\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>"
}

